    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14603" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπωθεν</span></b>  (in late Poets also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπωθε</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Q.S.
			6.647
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			7.172
		</span></i> (Antip. Sid.)), Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from afar</i> or <i>afar,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1206
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				816
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				674
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1184
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἄπωθεν</span>”
				<i>strangers, outsiders,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1371a12
				</span></i>
			, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen.,
				<i>far from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					108
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				674
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.111
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				1.12
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄποθεν.</span></div>
